":[{"changed_paths":["instrumentation/influxdb-2.4/javaagent/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/influxdb/v2_4/InfluxDbQueryState.java","instrumentation/influxdb-2.4/javaagent/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/influxdb/v2_4/InfluxDbQueryLifecycleTest.java"],"commit":"91669ba1f1a6e3d1d21297a08823c5269c56c6c5","parent":"fb119ad01453c0e4842a21752c5ebdc834c80cb7","patch_sha256":"93c9d743b777a2440601ffe73d7937006d9adcf7a874d0b302373def6c48ad97","subject":"Fix canceled MessagePack query read telemetry","tree":"ee13f75a00dc1bec20f37912d5f0ad69977553f8"}],"cumulative_patch_sha256":"93c9d743b777a2440601ffe73d7937006d9adcf7a874d0b302373def6c48ad97","finding_commits":{"review:5580641996":"91669ba1f1a6e3d1d21297a08823c5269c56c6c5"},"parent":"fb119ad01453c0e4842a21752c5ebdc834c80cb7","patch_sha256":"93c9d743b777a2440601ffe73d7937006d9adcf7a874d0b302373def6c48ad97","tree":"ee13f75a00dc1bec20f37912d5f0ad69977553f8"},"dispositions":{"findings":[{"analysis":"Confirmed in both influxdb-java 2.14 and 2.25: MessagePackTraverser wraps read IOExceptions in InfluxDBException, bypassing the cancellation filter and retaining a false failure. The filter now recognizes that exact wrapper with an immediate IOException cause only for canceled calls. A class-name check preserves compatibility because InfluxDBException is absent in 2.4. Agent-backed regressions verify blocked MessagePack reads with and without failure consumers produce successful spans and duration metrics, while MessagePack decoding failures and separately captured user callback exceptions, including the same wrapped-IOException shape after cancellation, remain failures. All 14 lifecycle cases pass against both 2.14 and 2.25; the non-Docker 2.4 statement-error compatibility test and focused style checks also pass. The frozen description remains accurate.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"review:5580641996"}],"input_identity":{},"outcome":"fixes","request_digest":"968be677a16bfbc73abdba71e91582614fabf1c19e37d92bbba4c05b946e1d21","schema":2},"download_sha256":"ecfe79d09c81f070b154be1599a65059fbc8136a71cfd79cd781c18509d3d24c","frozen_sha":"fb119ad01453c0e4842a21752c5ebdc834c80cb7","pr":20703,"publication_eligible":false,"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","request_digest":"968be677a16bfbc73abdba71e91582614fabf1c19e37d92bbba4c05b946e1d21","request_id":"8f5b49f0920b454b93b99206a82ee17f","run_attempt":1,"run_id":39368641862,"schema":2,"scope":"Structural/Git verification only. No target code or tests are executed.","server_artifact_digest":"sha256:ecfe79d09c81f070b154be1599a65059fbc8136a71cfd79cd781c18509d3d24c","verification":"verified","verification_run":{"attempt":1,"id":39371610466},"workflow_revision":"702f9d0316fccd229b4e90e9a01723d297e91b81"},"request":{"authorized_actor_id":218610,"baseline_review_ids":[5566618546,5566651972,5566713561,5577451717,5578038543,5578376761,5580015794,5580024701,5580039812,5580084717,5580599974,5580641996],"budgets":{"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udd35 Needs a closer look\n\nIntentional cancellation during a blocked MessagePack read can still produce erroneous failure telemetry.\n\n**No open issues** \ud83c\udf89\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>1 previously missed issue</strong></summary>\n\nIn code that hasn't changed since last review\n\n<details>\n<summary><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> Suppress telemetry for canceled blocked MessagePack reads</summary>\n\n`instrumentation/\u200binfluxdb-2.4/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200bmain/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200binfluxdb/\u200bv2_4/\u200bInfluxDbQueryState.java:59`\n\n[Javaagent] Canceling a blocked MessagePack chunk read still produces failure telemetry. In influxdb-java 2.14 and 2.25, `MessagePackTraverser` wraps read `IOException`s in `InfluxDBException`. The chunk-processor advice passes that wrapper here, so this guard saves it despite cancellation; `endResponse()` then retains it through `callbackError`, producing an ERROR span and error-tagged duration. Recognize this specific wrapped read failure as well as direct `IOException`s, while leaving decoding failures and separately captured user-callback exceptions intact. Add a MessagePack regression that cancels while a chunk read is blocked.\n</details>\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>1 resolved since last review</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Add regression test for chunked-query decoding failure capture](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20703#discussion_r4320869073)\n</details>\n\n<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5580641996","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5580641996}],"frozen_at":1792469577,"frozen_at_iso":"2026-10-20T04:12:57Z","frozen_sha":"fb119ad01453c0e4842a21752c5ebdc834c80cb7","head_ref":"copilot/split-20685-influxdb","head_repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","head_repo_id":210933087,"input_mode":"direct","launch_run":{"actor_id":218610,"attempt":1,"id":39363887052},"loop_kind":"copilot_review","metadata":{"body":"<!--\nCHANGELOG.md is generated from merged pull requests. Do not add an entry unless this PR introduces\na deprecation or breaking change.\n-->\n\nSplits the InfluxDB changes from #20685, correcting query outcomes and duration timing without changing other integrations.\n\n- **Error classification:** Classify HTTP-200 top-level and per-statement errors with bounded `error.type`, never raw error text. Retain available HTTP error codes.\n- **Terminal completion:** End asynchronous and chunked operations exactly once after callbacks and chunk processing finish, retaining callback, transport, and decoding failures, including newer-client decoding failures without a failure consumer.\n- **Cancellation and compatibility:** Make the call available before failure consumers run so pre-response cancellation remains successful. Preserve `DONE` handling, callback parent context, and supported 2.4 APIs.\n- **Regression coverage:** Cover synchronous response errors, one asynchronous statement error, successful and failed chunked completion, cancellation before and after response delivery, callback failures after cancellation, and a single 2.4 statement-error case, with span and duration-metric assertions. Retain HTTP `400` assertions in the existing failing-query integration test.","title":"Fix InfluxDB query error classification and async completion"},"mode":"publish","pr":20703,"pr_author_id":198982749,"protocol":"git-candidate-v1","publication":{"auth_mode":"fine_grained_pat","authorized_actor_id":218610,"authorized_at":1792466522,"generation":5,"max_pipelines":5,"phase":"b80041c4df3c4d05a0856e28fcb1d087","profile":"git-candidate-v1","required_checks":[]},"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","repo_i